{"path":"container/inplace_vector/unchecked_emplace_back","title":"std::inplace_vector<T,N>::unchecked_emplace_back","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::inplace_vector&lt;T,N&gt;::</span>unchecked_emplace_back","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/inplace_vector/unchecked_emplace_back","section":"container","kind":"page","summary":"Appends a new element to the end of the container. Typically, the element is constructed using placement-new to construct the element in-place at the location provided by the container.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx26\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> <span class=\"kw1\">class</span>... <span class=\"me1\">Args</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><br><span class=\"kw4\">constexpr</span> reference unchecked_emplace_back<span class=\"br0\">(</span> Args<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;&amp;</span>... <span class=\"me1\">args</span> <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx26\">(since C++26)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Appends a new element to the end of the container. Typically, the element is constructed using placement-<span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">new</span> to construct the element in-place at the location provided by the container. The arguments <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">args...</span></code> are forwarded to the constructor as <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/forward\"><span class=\"kw1125\">std::<span class=\"me2\">forward</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>Args<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>args<span class=\"br0\">)</span>...</span></code>.\nEquivalent to <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">return</span> <span class=\"sy2\">*</span>try_emplace_back<span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/forward\"><span class=\"kw1125\">std::<span class=\"me2\">forward</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>Args<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>args<span class=\"br0\">)</span>...<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></code>.\n</p><p>Before the call to this function <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">size<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> capacity<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> must be <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw2\">true</span></span></code>. Otherwise, the behavior is undefined.\n</p><p>No iterators or references are invalidated, except <a href=\"/w/cpp/container/inplace_vector/end\"><code>end()</code></a>, which is invalidated if the insertion occurs.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> args\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> arguments to forward to the constructor of the element\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-par-hitem\">\n<td colspan=\"3\"> Type requirements\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-par-req\">\n<td colspan=\"3\"> -<div class=\"spacer\"></div><code>T</code> must be <a href=\"/w/cpp/named_req/EmplaceConstructible\"><em class=\"t-named-req\">EmplaceConstructible</em></a> into <code>inplace_vector</code> from <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/forward\"><span class=\"kw1125\">std::<span class=\"me2\">forward</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>Args<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>args<span class=\"br0\">)</span>...</span></code>.\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p><a href=\"/w/cpp/container/inplace_vector/back\"><code>back()</code></a>, i.e. a reference to the inserted element.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Complexity\">Complexity</h3>\n<p>Constant.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Exceptions\">Exceptions</h3>\n<p>Any exception thrown by initialization of inserted element. If an exception is thrown for any reason, this function has no effect (<a href=\"/w/cpp/language/exceptions#Exception_safety\">strong exception safety guarantee</a>).\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<div class=\"t-notice\">This section is incomplete<br>Reason: Explain the purpose of this API. </div>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;inplace_vector&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;new&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;print&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;string&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;utility&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/container/inplace_vector\"><span class=\"kw3363\">std::<span class=\"me2\">inplace_vector</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/pair\"><span class=\"kw1104\">std::<span class=\"me2\">pair</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/string/basic_string\"><span class=\"kw1238\">std::<span class=\"me2\">string</span></span></a>, <a href=\"/w/cpp/string/basic_string\"><span class=\"kw1238\">std::<span class=\"me2\">string</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">2</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> fauna<span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/string/basic_string\"><span class=\"kw1238\">std::<span class=\"me2\">string</span></span></a> dog<span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"st0\">\"<span class=\"es1\">\\N</span>{DOG}\"</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    fauna.<span class=\"me1\">unchecked_emplace_back</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"<span class=\"es1\">\\N</span>{CAT}\"</span>, dog<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    fauna.<span class=\"me1\">unchecked_emplace_back</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"<span class=\"es1\">\\N</span>{CAT}\"</span>, std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">move</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>dog<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/println\"><span class=\"kw3402\">std::<span class=\"me2\">println</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"fauna = {}\"</span>, fauna<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <span class=\"co1\">// fauna.unchecked_emplace_back(\"BUG\", \"BUG\"); // undefined behavior: no space</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>fauna = [(\"🐈\", \"🐕\"), (\"🐈\", \"🐕\")]</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/container/inplace_vector/emplace_back\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>emplace_back</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  constructs an element in-place at the end <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/container/inplace_vector/append_range\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>append_range</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  adds a range of elements to the end <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/container/inplace_vector/push_back\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>push_back</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  adds an element to the end <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/container/inplace_vector/try_push_back\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>try_push_back</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  tries to add an element to the end <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/container/inplace_vector/try_emplace_back\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>try_emplace_back</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  tries to construct an element in-place at the end <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/container/inplace_vector/try_append_range\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>try_append_range</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  tries to add a range of elements to the end <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/container/inplace_vector/unchecked_push_back\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>unchecked_push_back</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  unconditionally adds an element to the end <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/container/inplace_vector/pop_back\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>pop_back</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  removes the last element <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/iterator/back_inserter\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>back_inserter</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  creates a <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/iterator/back_insert_iterator\">std::back_insert_iterator</a></span> of type inferred from the argument <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function template)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Complexity","id":"Complexity"},{"depth":3,"text":"Exceptions","id":"Exceptions"},{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"container","title":"Containers library"},{"path":"container/inplace_vector","title":"std::inplace_vector"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::inplace_vector<T,N>::unchecked_emplace_back","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration; revisions: since C++26. Appends a new element to the end of the container."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"args"},{"label":"Return value","note":"back(), i.e. a reference to the inserted element."},{"label":"Complexity","note":"Constant."},{"label":"Exceptions","note":"Any exception thrown by initialization of inserted element."},{"label":"Notes"},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"emplace_back","note":"constructs an element in-place at the end"},{"label":"append_range","note":"adds a range of elements to the end"},{"label":"push_back","note":"adds an element to the end"},{"label":"try_push_back","note":"tries to add an element to the end"},{"label":"try_emplace_back","note":"tries to construct an element in-place at the end"},{"label":"+4 more"}]}]},"standards":["C++26"],"wordCount":306,"codeBlockCount":2}
